<title>USA: Coastal to repurchase $1.2 bln debt.</title>
<headline>Coastal to repurchase $1.2 bln debt.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Coastal Corp said on</p>
<p>Tuesday it offered to purchase certain of its debt issues with</p>
<p>a total principal amount outstanding of $1.2 billion.</p>
<p>Issues affected include:</p>
<p>			 Amount			Reference    Fixed</p>
<p> Security Issue  Outstanding     Cusip	 Note	 Sread</p>
<p>10-3/8% Senior</p>
<p>Notes due</p>
<p>  Oct. 1, 2000   $250 million   190441 AJ4  5-3/4% U.S.</p>
<p>							 Treasury Note 0.36%</p>
<p>							  due 10/2000</p>
<p>10% Senior</p>
<p>Notes due</p>
<p>  Feb. 1, 2001   $300 million   190441 AL9  5-5/8% U.S.</p>
<p>							 Treasury Note</p>
<p>							  due 2/2001   0.39%</p>
<p>9-3/4% Senior</p>
<p>Debentures due</p>
<p>  Aug. 1, 2003   $300 million   190441 AM7   5-3/4% U.S.</p>
<p>							 Treasury note 0.44%</p>
<p>							    due 8/2003</p>
<p>10-1/4% Senior</p>
<p>Debentures due</p>
<p>  Oct. 15, 2004   $200 million   190441 AH8   7-7/8% U.S.</p>
<p>							   Treasury Note</p>
<p>							   due 11/2004 0.49%</p>
<p>10-3/4% Senior</p>
<p>Debentures due</p>
<p>  Oct. 1, 2010    $150 million   190441 AK1   6-1/2% U.S.</p>
<p>							    Treasury Note</p>
<p>							  due 10/2006  0.68%</p>
<p>The company said the tender offer would remain open from January 29 until February 7, but Coastal said it reserved the right to extend the offer. Coastal said the repurchase would be financed through various credit facilities and available cash.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
